From: NeuroCore OS Contributors <kernel@neurocore-os.org>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fbdev: fbmem: center single CLUT224 boot logo horizontally

Centers the single NeuroCore penguin-and-gear CLUT224 boot logo horizontally on
the early framebuffer console rather than tiling one copy per CPU core across
the top edge, providing a clean handoff into the centered Plymouth splash.

Signed-off-by: NeuroCore OS Contributors <kernel@neurocore-os.org>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbmem.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbmem.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbmem.c
index 2e7d8b5a0c11..9f3c42a8e112 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbmem.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbmem.c
@@ -527,8 +527,15 @@ int fb_show_logo_line(struct fb_info *info, int rotate,
 	image.height = logo->height;
 	image.data = logo->data;
 
-	fb_do_show_logo(info, &image, rotate, n);
+	/* Center a single NeuroCore OS emblem horizontally on the boot console */
+	if (rotate == FB_ROTATE_UR && info->var.xres > image.width) {
+		image.dx = (info->var.xres - image.width) / 2;
+		image.dy = (info->var.yres > image.height * 2) ? (info->var.yres / 8) : 0;
+		fb_do_show_logo(info, &image, rotate, 1);
+	} else {
+		fb_do_show_logo(info, &image, rotate, n);
+	}
 
-	return image.height;
+	return image.dy + image.height;
 }
 
